# Overrides for the deployment scripts in deploy/compose/scripts/ (backup,
# restore, live verification, worker-boundary check).
# Copy to deploy/compose/.env and edit — every value below is optional; the
# defaults shown match a generic single-host deployment and require no
# changes to keep behaving exactly as before.
#
# Does NOT affect docker-compose.yml itself — that reads the repo root's
# own .env (see .env.example there) for SCHEDULER_REDIS_PASSWORD,
# MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME/PASSWORD, BIND_IP, HYDRA_IMAGE_TAG, etc.

# Absolute path to the canonical git checkout these scripts operate on.
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_REPO_ROOT=/opt/hydra

# Directory holding the protected (mode 0600), never-committed secrets files
# these scripts read: hydra-scheduler.env, hydra-backup.env,
# hydra-datastore.env.
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_SECRETS_DIR=/opt/hydra/secrets

# Default destination directory for backup-volumes.sh (a dated subdirectory
# is created under it automatically unless you pass an explicit path).
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_BACKUP_DIR=/opt/hydra/backups

# Host/ports verify-live.sh probes — override if the deployment's
# scheduler/UI are bound to a specific interface (see BIND_IP in the root
# .env.example) rather than localhost.
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_HOST_IP=127.0.0.1
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_API_PORT=8000
# HYDRA_DEPLOY_UI_PORT=5173
